.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_ENCODER_TO_BIO 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_ENCODER_to_data ,
.Nm OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio ,
.Nm OSSL_ENCODER_to_fp
.Nd Routines to perform an encoding
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/encoder.h
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_ENCODER_to_data
.Fa "OSSL_ENCODER_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "unsigned char **pdata"
.Fa "size_t *pdata_len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio
.Fa "OSSL_ENCODER_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_ENCODER_to_fp
.Fa "OSSL_ENCODER_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "FILE *fp"
.Fc
Feature availability macros:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It OSSL_ENCODER_to_fp() is only available when Ar OPENSSL_NO_STDIO No is undefined.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_data
runs the encoding process for the context
.Fa ctx ,
with the output going to the
.Em *pdata
and
.Em *pdata_len .
If
.Em *pdata
is NULL when
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_data
is called, a buffer will be allocated using
.Xr OPENSSL_zalloc 3 ,
and
.Em *pdata
will be set to point at the start of that buffer, and
.Em *pdata_len
will be assigned its length when
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_data
returns.
If
.Em *pdata
is non-NULL when
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_data
is called,
.Em *pdata_len
is assumed to have its size.
In this case,
.Em *pdata
will be set to point after the encoded bytes, and
.Em *pdata_len
will be assigned the number of remaining bytes.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio
runs the encoding process for the context
.Fa ctx ,
with the output going to the
.Vt BIO
.Fa out .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_fp
does the same thing as
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio ,
except that the output is going to the
.Vt FILE
.Fa fp .
.Pp
For
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio
and
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_fp ,
the application is required to set up the
.Vt BIO
or
.Vt FILE
properly, for example to have it in text or binary mode as is
appropriate for the encoder output type.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio ,
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_fp
and
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_to_data
return 1 on success, or 0 on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To encode a pkey as PKCS#8 with PEM format into a bio:
.Bd -literal
 OSSL_ENCODER_CTX *ectx;
 const char *format = "PEM";
 const char *structure = "PrivateKeyInfo"; /* PKCS#8 structure */
 const unsigned char *pass = "my password";

 ectx = OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_new_for_pkey(pkey,
                                      OSSL_KEYMGMT_SELECT_KEYPAIR
                                      | OSSL_KEYMGMT_SELECT_DOMAIN_PARAMETERS,
                                      format, structure,
                                      NULL);
 if (ectx == NULL) {
     /* error: no suitable potential encoders found */
 }
 if (pass != NULL)
     OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_set_passphrase(ectx, pass, strlen(pass));
 if (OSSL_ENCODER_to_bio(ectx, bio)) {
     /* pkey was successfully encoded into the bio */
 } else {
     /* encoding failure */
 }
 OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_free(ectx);
.Ed
.Pp
To encode a pkey as PKCS#8 with DER format encrypted with AES-256-CBC
into a buffer:
.Bd -literal
 OSSL_ENCODER_CTX *ectx;
 const char *format = "DER";
 const char *structure = "PrivateKeyInfo"; /* PKCS#8 structure */
 const unsigned char *pass = "my password";
 unsigned char *data = NULL;
 size_t datalen;

 ectx = OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_new_for_pkey(pkey,
                                      OSSL_KEYMGMT_SELECT_KEYPAIR
                                      | OSSL_KEYMGMT_SELECT_DOMAIN_PARAMETERS,
                                      format, structure,
                                      NULL);
 if (ectx == NULL) {
     /* error: no suitable potential encoders found */
 }
 if (pass != NULL) {
     OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_set_passphrase(ectx, pass, strlen(pass));
     OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_set_cipher(ctx, "AES-256-CBC", NULL);
 }
 if (OSSL_ENCODER_to_data(ectx, &data, &datalen)) {
     /*
      * pkey was successfully encoded into a newly allocated
      * data buffer
      */
 } else {
     /* encoding failure */
 }
 OSSL_ENCODER_CTX_free(ectx);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr provider 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_ENCODER_CTX 3
.Sh HISTORY
The functions described here were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
